{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "036V", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$X' \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n0 \\to f^*\\Omega_{X/Y} \\to \\Omega_{X'/Y} \\to \\Omega_{X'/X} \\to 0.\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$X' \\to Y$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Omega_{X/Y} = 0$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\to Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-properties-morphisms-local-source}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-unramified-characterize}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-composition-unramified}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-etale-smooth-unramified}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-local-source-fppf-algebra}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-flat-finitely-presented-permanence-algebra}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-triangle-differentials-smooth}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-unramified-omega-zero}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{lemma-properties-morphisms-local-source}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "SPACE_0004": "\\ ", "SPACE_0005": "\\ ", "SPACE_0006": "\\ ", "SPACE_0007": "\\ ", "SPACE_0008": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:abf8cd207eac203a6ab6e5fd1dc5c115665ff6bdef88f0da521d198a1d4a0234", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0d54ec6c6248e32a53d094bf82c4d560d21824680a03a7d6e61ce5b896caf6c8", "source_text": "We are going to use\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nBy\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe property of being unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>G-unramified)\nis local for Zariski on source and target. By\nMorphisms, Lemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004>\nwe see the precomposition\nof an unramified (resp.<SPACE_0002>G-unramified) morphism by an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is\nunramified (resp.<SPACE_0003>G-unramified).\nFinally, suppose that <MATH_0001> is a morphism of affine schemes\nand that <MATH_0002> is a surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism of affine schemes\nsuch that <MATH_0003> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0004>G-unramified).\nThen <MATH_0004> is of finite type (resp.<SPACE_0005>finite presentation), and by\nLemma <REF_0005>\n(resp.<SPACE_0006>Lemma <REF_0006>)\nwe see that <MATH_0005> is of finite type (resp.<SPACE_0007>finite presentation) also. By\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0007>\nwe have a short exact sequence\n<MATH_0006>\nAs <MATH_0007> is unramified we see that the middle term is zero.\nHence, as <MATH_0008> is faithfully flat we see that <MATH_0009>.\nHence <MATH_0010> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0008>G-unramified), see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0008>.\nThis proves the last assumption of\nLemma <REF_0009>\nand finishes the proof.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:99b89ef6c7ed8bcb7bd051322b22fe86499fa9c38c8ed7d33322222a3977b4fd", "unit_id": "tag:03YV:proof"}
